<div class="lead">
  <p>Need to extract images from a PDF or convert document pages to pictures? Whether you're creating presentations, sharing specific pages, or need images for a website, converting PDF to JPG is a common task.</p>
  <p>In this guide, I'll walk you through the best free methods and help you choose the right tool for your needs.</p>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>Why Convert PDF to JPG?</h2>
  <p>There are many reasons you might need to convert a PDF to JPG images:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Presentations:</strong> Add PDF pages as slides without the PDF viewer</li>
    <li><strong>Social media:</strong> Share individual pages on Instagram, LinkedIn, or Twitter</li>
    <li><strong>Web content:</strong> Use PDF pages as images on websites</li>
    <li><strong>Thumbnails:</strong> Create preview images for document galleries</li>
    <li><strong>Legacy documents:</strong> Convert old PDFs to images for easier viewing</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How to Convert PDF to JPG Online</h2>
  <p>Our free converter works entirely in your browser - no software needed.</p>

  <ol>
    <li>Visit our <a href="/en/tools/pdf-to-jpg/">PDF to JPG converter</a></li>
    <li>Upload your PDF (up to 50MB)</li>
    <li>Choose which pages to convert (or convert all)</li>
    <li>Download individual images or all as a ZIP file</li>
  </ol>

  <p>The converter produces high-quality 300 DPI images suitable for printing and professional use.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Understanding Image Quality</h2>
  <p>When converting PDF to JPG, quality matters. Here's what affects the output:</p>

  <h3>Resolution (DPI)</h3>
  <p>Our converter outputs at 300 DPI (dots per inch), which is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Perfect for printing</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Clear when zoomed</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Suitable for professional documents</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Color vs. Grayscale</h3>
  <p>Color PDFs convert to full-color JPGs. If you need smaller file sizes, consider converting to grayscale - you'll often get 70-80% smaller files.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Pro Tips</h2>

  <h3>Convert Specific Pages Only</h3>
  <p>Don't need the whole document? Enter page numbers like "1,3,5" or ranges like "1-5" to convert only what you need. This saves time and produces smaller downloads.</p>

  <h3>Use ZIP for Multiple Pages</h3>
  <p>Converting a 20-page PDF? Download all images as a single ZIP file instead of downloading 20 separate files.</p>

  <h3>Consider File Size</h3>
  <p>High-resolution JPGs can be large. After conversion, use our <a href="/en/tools/compress-pdf/">Compress tool</a> on individual images if needed.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>When to Use Other Formats</h2>
  <p>JPG isn't always the best choice. Consider these alternatives:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>PNG</strong> - For images with text (better compression for simple graphics)</li>
    <li><strong>WebP</strong> - For web use (smaller files, same quality)</li>
    <li><strong>SVG</strong> - If the PDF contains vector graphics</li>
  </ul>
</section>